r chewing.", "tags": ["uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Tobacco and the plant valerian are also considered to be anaphrodisiac in their effects, diminishing sexual inclination.", "reference": "1961, Harry E. Wedeck, Dictionary of Aphrodisiacs, New York: The Citadel Press, page 11:"}, {"text": "Tobacco-settlement bonds are a tribute both to the inventiveness of bankers and the childlike impatience of politicians.", "reference": "2013 September 7, “Unlucky strike”, in The Economist, volume 408, number 8852, archived from the original on 04 Aug 2020:"}, {"text": "City councilors in Newton have approved a generational ban on tobacco and e-cigarette sales in the city that will prohibit purchases by anyone born after March 1, 2004, joining a growing number of Massachusetts communities that have passed measures to curb tobacco use among young people.", "reference": "2025 January 22, Nick Stoico, “Newton city council approves generational tobacco ban, joining other Mass. towns”, in Boston Globe, archived from the original on 23 Jan 2025:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(countable) A variety of tobacco.", "tags": ["countable"], "examples": ["Tobaccos from the Connecticut Valley were used for wrapping cigars."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "tupakkalajike"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "tupakkalaatu"}], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/təˈbæk.əʊ/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/təˈbæk.oʊ/", "tags": ["US"]}], "forms": [{"word": "tobaccos", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "tobaccoing", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "tobaccoed", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "tobaccoed